There have been lots and lots of suggestions for new monsters, new weapons,
armors, rooms, ways of making the game harder, and ways of eliminating abuse.
Unfortunately, I'm going to do pretty much the same. Rather than trying to
limit how items are used (i.e. polypiling, wishing for a wand of wishing,
cursed genociding monsters, area of influence for ring of conflict, etc.),
I suggest letting the game get harder when these things are done. That way
if people don't want to do this, they will benefit from it, and if they do
want to do it, they speed the digging of their own graves.

Let items that can be abused carry an abuse factor which accumulates as the
abuses take place. For example, if you polymorph 3 items on separate spots,
no problem. But if you polymorph 5 piles of 20 items each, you add points to
your abuse total, say 1 point for each item in a pile larger than 5 (i.e. then
the above example would add 15+15+15+15+15 to you total). Wishing for a wand
of wishing would add some amount of abuse points (times the number of charges).
Using a ring of conflict in a room with say more than 4 monsters adds an abuse
point for each monster more than 4 every turn. All these values were chosen
without much consideration for how large they should be.

Now what happens when you total gets to a certain amount. Then the evil god of
abuse sends an abuse demon to battle you. This demon should be incredibly tough
relative to the player (i.e. a level three player shouldn't get a demon with
100 hp, 3 attacks, AC -5, but a demon should always be tougher than the
player). Make the demon immune to all magic, so that the player has to fight
it or run away. If the player has speed boots, let the demon move at double
normal speed. The idea is not encounter these demons at all, and not to do
abuse so that they appear. I think an interesting twist would be that the
demon can make a steal attack (i.e. like a nymph) with the stolen item gone
for good (i.e. if you kill the demon, what it stole will not be there).

Lastly, make the abuse limit so that it will allow 2 or 3 normal abuses (i.e.
polypiles). Each time a demon appears the total is made 0, but the limit is
halved. The more a player abuses (to make the game easy) the more demons
appear (it gets hard). When players lose their artifacts and +5 armors,
permanently, they will think twice about abusing. We don't want to remove it,
just deter it.

Lastly (again), allow sacrifices of items which cause abuse to lower abuse
points, or send the demon away (an alternative would be to give the demon
such items). This way when a player abuses without realizing (not everyone
reads the spoilers to make the game easier), he can get out of it without
dying. The abuse demon could say something to the effect of "give me <item>
as payment for you abuse, or die!" This item could be the first targeted for
steal attack.

Well, maybe most people will think this idea stinks (probably those who
abuse a lot), and maybe it does, but it will allow players do "skate on thin
ice." Most of the other suggestions either allow abuse outright or not at all
(I don't mean to imply that the suggestions may not be the best).

Tom


